  "data": {
    "body": "A population's size at time $t$ is $x(t)$ and is modeled by the differential equation\n\\[\n\\frac{dx}{dt} = \\frac{1}{3} x (x - 3).\n\\]\n\n(a) Sketch a phase diagram for the differential equation. What does this phase diagram tell you about $\\lim_{t \\to \\infty} x(t)$ if $x(0) = 1$?\n(b) Find an explicit solution to the differential equation when $x(0) = 1$.",
    "solution": "(a) $\\lim_{t\\to\\infty} x(t) = 0$.\n(b) $x=\\frac{3}{1+2e^t}$",
